WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.901
-Back to a talk-show audience
chair situation.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:06.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah! Exactly right!

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.234
It feels good, doesn't it?
-Oh, it feels amazing.

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:10.434
The energy of humans.
-Feel the energy, exactly right!

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:11.868
-Oh, it's so good!
-We've missed it.

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.234
-Hello! Look!
Look at that!

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.167
Look at that!
-Yeah, we're real.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.934
We're not Zooming!
We're not Zooming! Yeah.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.400
I have to talk to you about
this, your song.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.634
But, yeah, I mean --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.701
-Hi, guys!

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:28.601
-First, I want to get to,
the eighth and final season

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.367
of "Black-ish" is airing now.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.234
By the way, what a season.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.400
-It's coming along well.
-What a season already.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.434
-What a season, Jimmy!
-What a season!

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:38.334
What a season!
-Way to take it out!

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:40.868
-What a season this one, whoa.
-Hey!

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:44.534
-Now, recently we had
Anthony Anderson on the show.

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:45.634
We love --
-Oh, I know him.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:46.934
-Yes, you know him, yeah.
-I know him.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.901
-Of course you know him, yeah.
And I was saying --

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.167
-Nice fella.
-A nice dude.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:54.267
I go, "Are you gonna get
emotional when you say goodbye?"

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.667
And he's like, "Oh,
maybe a little, not really."

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.400
I don't know if he will.
Did he get emotional?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.968
Did you get emotional?
-I was a mess.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.734
-Yeah, of course!
-So, well, it was amazing.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.467
Knowing that you're walking
into the end is, like,

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:09.267
a really beautiful thing,
so I felt very open-hearted.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.167
The whole last season,
I was aware.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.434
Like, "Okay.
I'm gonna take this in.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:14.767
I love this.
This is hard, but I love it."

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:17.300
And then, the last week,
I gave myself permission

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.567
to just, you know, let it fly.

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.634
-Wow.
-And I cried a lot,

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.767
to the point that Anthony,
at some points, was like,

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:25.501
"Seriously?
You're doing this again?"

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:27.400
[ Laughter ]
I was like, "Yes, Anthony.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.634
It's the end, and I'm sad."
And then the last scene we shot

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.634
was a scene
between just Anthony and I.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:34.934
I can't say what was happening,

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.734
and I could not
get through rehearsal.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.868
You know when you have
that cry that, like,

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:40.234
you feel like your neck's
gonna explode?

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.200
Like, I was like --
[ Sobbing ]

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.167
I was like, "Just do it!
Just -- Just do it!

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.934
Just block it out,
and I'll deliver the scene!"

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.234
I was a mess.
-A mess.

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:52.701
-A mess.
-I mean, it's such a great show.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:55.000
-I mean, eight years,
and, you know, you spend, like,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.934
so much time with everybody.
-It's your family.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.834
-It's your family.
I mean, I spent more time

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:00.701
pretending I was married
to Anthony than not.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.100
-Yeah. Isn't that funny?
-You know what I mean?

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.634
And you're with them 5:00 in the
morning till late at night,

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:06.634
and, you know...
-And working on the script,

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:07.901
and Kenya Barris,
who we love, and --

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:10.200
-Yeah, and the kids.
We watched them grow up.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.300
I fell like there were two
things that helped me

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.100
remember that
the time was passing --

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.300
the kids growing
and Anthony's facial hair.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.801
-Yeah, yeah, yeah,
those things changed.

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.567
-Because by the end,
he was like ZZ Top.

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:22.968
[ Laughter ]
He was like...

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.601
-He did have a good giant beard.
-He's like, "Hello.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:28.200
My name is Dre Johnson."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.000
-But we were talking about
the cameos that you had.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.334
No big deal.
Michelle Obama.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.901
-Who?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.901 --> 00:02:38.200
-Hello!
Michelle Obama.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.968
-Ms. Former First Lady.
Forever First Lady!

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.133
-Yes. But here's the thing
that Anthony said.

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:44.467
He said that
you got her to come on

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:46.067
'cause you texted her.
-I did.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.968
-Wait.
But did you actually text her?

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:53.133
-Yeah, we're friends.
[ Cheers ]

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.901
Shh.
"Don't tell nobody."

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:56.634
-"Don't tell anyone
that we're friends."

00:02:56.634 --> 00:03:00.400
-"Nobody, but I friends
with the lady."

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.234
-How did you guys
become friends?

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.200
-Well, I was an early campaigner

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.267
in 2007
when he was just a senator.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:07.934
And I always say I campaigned
for the Obamas,

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:09.834
but it was for Barack Obama,
who was,

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.701
you know, becoming president.
-Right.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:15.200
-And then, I became a part
of their mentor program,

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.501
so I worked with both of them
and went to the White House

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:20.234
a couple of times,
and then, you know, I --

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:21.868
I don't know.
I guess they liked me.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.901
-Oh, my God.
Oh, my God.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.200
-I don't know.
And they were like,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.767
"Yes, Michelle Obama
wants to be friends."

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:27.901
I was like,
"Has she been vetted?

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:29.501
I don't know who that is."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:32.801
"I don't remember her."
-Do you call her First Lady?

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:35.000
Do you call her Michelle?
-I was raised in the generation

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.767
where your teachers
and your friends' parents

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:37.901
are mister and missus.
-Of course.

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.200
-So in public,
she is Mrs. Obama,

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.234
she's former First Lady,
there's no question.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:45.200
I was calling her that also
as my friend, and she was like,

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.267
"Seriously, this has to stop."
And I was like,

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.567
"Okay, Mrs. Obama."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.701
And I curtsied as I did it.

00:03:50.701 --> 00:03:53.167
And then she was like,
"This has got to stop."

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:55.334
I was like, "Yes, Mrs. Obama."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:58.934
And we were doing a conversation
for the United States of Women,

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.734
and in front of the audience,
she was like,

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:03.634
"Seriously,
you have to call me Michelle."

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.801
And so, by the end
of the interview, I was like,

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:08.567
"Michelle," and the entire
audience was like, "Finally!"

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:09.734
-"Finally, you did it!

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.267
Finally,
you called her Michelle!"

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.334
-Out of respect, my goodness.
-She's the coolest.

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:15.267
-Oh, beyond. Beyond.
-The greatest.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:17.501
-Yeah. You know we have
things in common, Jimmy?

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.567
-Yeah, you do, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:22.734
-Well, you really are
an entrepreneur, by the way.

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:25.200
-Oh, yes, yes, yes, and a CEO.
-CEO, but --

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
You're not fooling around.

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:27.801
The real deal!
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:29.133
-Congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.033
-We talked about this
on the show, to just get

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:33.100
something launched, by the way,
it takes years

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.567
before you even
get to launch it.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.467
-It took 10 years for me to get
the company off the ground.

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.234
-Yeah. See?
No one knows that.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:40.868
-10 years of a lot of nos
and a lot of --

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:43.601
But I really believe in what
we're doing at Pattern,

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:46.100
which is exceeding the needs
of the curly, coily,

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.000
and tight-textured community.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.434
And we are a company
that is centered around

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:54.868
the celebration of Black beauty.
And that is an area

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:57.701
that needed help and support,
not because we do

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.434
but because the industry did.
-Yeah.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:01.501
-And so it has taken off,
and it's beautiful,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.767
and it's wonderful.
-Successful two years.

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:05.300
-PatternBeauty.com.
You gotta get your products.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.067
-Yeah!
You gotta get your products!

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.334
-Yeah. And then this.
-But then -- No, but then --

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:11.801
So just to have that
as successful, that's fantastic.

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:12.868
-Mm-hmm.
-Pattern Beauty,

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.100
and it's awesome,
what you're doing.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.834
But then you go,
"I'm gonna release a song."

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:18.734
-Yes, yes.
That's right, because why not?

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:19.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:23.901
So we are in Sephora Ulta
in Target.

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:26.300
So, you continue expanding
in the brand, and you think,

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.434
"What are other ways
that we can continue getting

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:29.601
the information out there?"

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:31.901
And I believe that hair care
is self-care.

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:34.300
And so the song is about
the ritual of hair care

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:38.701
as self-care and that authentic
legacy that we come from that --

00:05:38.701 --> 00:05:40.100
where you sit down
between the legs of your mother

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.334
and you get your hair done.
So...

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:43.968
♪ Sit down between
the legs of your mother ♪

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:45.534
♪ Your sister, your auntie ♪

00:05:45.534 --> 00:05:49.267
♪ Remember the scent of grease,
oil sliding down your scalp ♪

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, no, no, no, no!

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:53.133
-Yes! Yes!
-No, no, no, no, no!

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:54.968
-Yes!
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:56.734
Oh, it's makes me
nervous and sweaty.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.167
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.167 --> 00:05:59.968
-Singing, singing.
-You're a great singer.

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:01.367
-Singing makes me
nervous and sweaty.

00:06:01.367 --> 00:06:02.634
-Sing-ging.
-Sing-ging.

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:05.801
-But you're a great singer.
But you must be nervous.

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:08.434
-I come from a legacy of quite
a powerhouse singer lady.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.968
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, I've heard of --

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:13.000
-Have you heard of her?
-I've heard of your mom, yeah.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.567
She's pretty much --
-Just a little global treasure.

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:17.501
-Oh, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:18.767
"No big deal.
My mom's Diana Ross."

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:19.767
-Whatever!
[ Cheers ]

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:20.968
-"Would you
like to sing something?"

00:06:20.968 --> 00:06:23.133
"Yeah, no, I'm good."
-I'm good.

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:25.200
-"Mom, yeah, she's got it."
-"Go ahead, Mom."

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.934
-Do you remember, at one of
your mother's concerts,

00:06:28.934 --> 00:06:31.200
she put you on the spot
to sing something?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.534
-As a child?
-As a child.

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:35.067
-Yeah.
-And you did not want to sing.

00:06:35.067 --> 00:06:37.367
-I said, "No, ma'am."
-No.

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:40.334
And do you remember this at all?
-I actually really do

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:42.467
because my sister, Rhonda,
sang no problem.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:44.033
-Yes.
-Yeah. I mean --

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:46.534
And my grandma was there,
who's no longer alive, yeah.

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:47.701
-We actually --
We have the clip.

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:49.901
'Cause I just wanted
to show you being you.

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.167
Watch this.
You're gonna freak.

00:06:51.167 --> 00:06:53.133
-Oh, you guys are gonna die.
-Hey!

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:54.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:56.734
Chudney, Rhonda and Tracee.

00:06:56.734 --> 00:06:57.801
Hey.

00:06:57.801 --> 00:06:59.367
Who wants to sing first?

00:06:59.367 --> 00:07:02.334
-♪ Make this world
a better place ♪

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:04.234
♪ If you can ♪

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:06.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.534
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:12.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:12.033 --> 00:07:13.934
-Giant glasses.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:16.234
I was just like,
"No, no, no, no, no."

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:18.000
-How cute, come on.
-I was so shy.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.534
-Yeah.
-I was so shy,

00:07:19.534 --> 00:07:24.267
and then I finally sang
at a talent show in high school,

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:27.334
and I started too high, and I --
my voice cracked.

00:07:27.334 --> 00:07:29.467
-Yeah.
-And the entire school was like,

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:31.901
"Tracee! Tracee!"
And my friend had to

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:34.100
come onstage and hug me,
and then I tried again,

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.100
and then I took a break
for 35 years.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:40.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:41.901
-Since you're a singer now,
I want to play

00:07:41.901 --> 00:07:44.133
a fun singing game with you
when we come back.

00:07:44.133 --> 00:07:46.133
Tracee Ellis Ross, everybody.

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:50.467
"Legacy" is available now
on all streaming platforms!

